&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Director of LV/Fiber Deployment leads the planning, execution, and operational handoff of low-voltage and fiber infrastructure deployments across data center, edge, and network facilities. This leader ensures deployments are delivered safely, on schedule, within budget, and to defined quality and reliability standards.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The role owns the end-to-end deployment lifecycle: design coordination, vendor strategy, material readiness, field execution, commissioning support, documentation, and turnover to operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll be Doing&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead regional or global deployment programs for structured cabling, fiber backbone, low-voltage systems, and related physical infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and lead a high-performing team of deployment managers, program managers, field engineers, and vendor partners.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own deployment planning, schedules, resource models, budgets, forecasts, and executive reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with design, construction, network engineering, data center operations, supply chain, security, and commissioning teams to deliver production-ready infrastructure.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Establish standardized deployment playbooks, quality controls, acceptance criteria, and turnover processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage installation partners and vendors, including selection, performance management, capacity planning, safety, quality, and commercial accountability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive deployment readiness by ensuring materials, labor, site access, permits, test equipment, and documentation are available ahead of execution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee fiber testing, labeling, documentation, as-built records, cable management, and remediation of quality issues.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead complex retrofits and live-site deployments while protecting customer availability, safety, and operational continuity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define and improve deployment KPIs, including on-time delivery, first-pass quality, cost per deployment, defect rates, safety performance, and time-to-service.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify deployment risks early, remove execution blockers, and lead escalation paths across internal and external stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You’ll Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10+ years of experience in physical infrastructure deployment, data centers, telecommunications, network construction, or large-scale critical environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;5+ years leading multi-site teams, contractors, vendors, or complex deployment programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep knowledge of structured cabling, fiber-optic infrastructure, low-voltage systems, testing and certification practices, and cable-management standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience delivering infrastructure in data centers, telecom networks, industrial facilities, or other mission-critical environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated success managing large vendor workforces, budgets, schedules, and quality programs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of construction, commissioning, change control, site readiness, and operational handoff.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to lead safely in live production environments and balance speed, quality, cost, and availability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent executive communication, cross-functional leadership, and problem-solving skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred Qualifications and Experience&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience supporting hyperscale cloud, AI/GPU infrastructure, or high-density data center deployments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with fiber design, OTDR testing, splice management, MPO/MTP systems, and structured-cabling standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with BICSI, TIA/EIA, ISO/IEC, and applicable local codes and safety requirements.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with deployment tooling, asset tracking, work-order systems, and dashboard-driven operational management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant certifications such as RCDD, CFOT, PMP, or Lean/Six Sigma.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Success Measures&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Safe, on-time, and on-budget deployment delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fiber and low-voltage installation quality and first-pass acceptance rates&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Reduction in deployment defects, rework, and time to operational handoff&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Vendor capacity, productivity, and performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deployment readiness and schedule predictability&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stakeholder satisfaction across construction, engineering, network, and operations teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;What We Can Offer You&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Nscale, you&#39;ll find a collaborative, supportive, and innovative environment where your contributions spark real impact. We&#39;re building something extraordinary, and we want you at the core.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Highly competitive package (base + bonus + equity) with reviews every 12 months. 🚀&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Join the fastest-growing tech startup — your chance to push boundaries, collaborate with brilliant minds, and make your mark on cutting-edge AI.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expect a dynamic progression plan tailored to your ambitions. Grow by trying new things, leading, challenging the status quo, and owning your impact, always with our full support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Human-First Flexibility: We treat you as humans first. 🫶🏽 Our flexible workplace trusts Nscalers to deliver.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
